# The osquery packages the core image ships to the servers of the customer (WP-26 slice 3, D-169 (10)). The core Containerfile sources this
# file (KEY=VALUE only, no spaces, quotes or $: a test holds it to that), downloads the five package files from the official release, checks each
# against the SHA-256 below BEFORE it copies it into the image, and fails the build on any mismatch. Nothing is downloaded at run time.
#
# OSQUERY_VERSION is one number with OSQUERY_VERSION in web/src/features/inventory/installScripts.ts and agentintake.OsqueryVersion
# (modules/agent-intake/install.go); TestInstall_VersionsAgree fails when they differ. To bump it: change the three together with the five
# package hashes in one commit, then `make core-image` (the build checks the hashes) and the local real-osqueryd run of
# .ai/deferred/feat-agent-intake-osquery.md.
#
# Source of the hashes (2026-11-11): the three files of the official release https://github.com/osquery/osquery/releases/tag/5.12.1
# (osquery_5.12.1-1.linux_amd64.deb 30579058 bytes, osquery-5.12.1-1.linux.x86_64.rpm 30439995 bytes, osquery-5.12.1.msi 18853888 bytes)
# downloaded over HTTPS from github.com/osquery/osquery/releases/download/5.12.1/ and hashed with sha256sum. The release publishes no checksum
# file and no asset digest (gh api repos/osquery/osquery/releases/tags/5.12.1: digest empty), so the same three files were also downloaded from the
# official package site (https://pkg.osquery.io/deb/, /rpm/, /windows/) and gave the same three hashes.
# The two arm64 Linux packages (D-399, 2026-11-13: osquery_5.12.1-1.linux_arm64.deb 28510972 bytes, osquery-5.12.1-1.linux.aarch64.rpm 28457612
# bytes) were pinned the same way: downloaded from the release and from https://pkg.osquery.io/deb/ and /rpm/, same hashes from both.
# Measured cost (2026-11-12, make core-image): the osquery layer is 79.9 MB, the whole core image 127 MB; the two arm64 packages add 57 MB (D-399).
OSQUERY_VERSION=5.12.1
